(PRC-17 — `Unmount "<target>".` performs umount2(2).
 Also covers: PRC-18 (`umount` is an accepted alias) and PRC-19 (`lazily`
 requests MNT_DETACH) — all four spellings are exercised.
 SAFETY / LIMIT: unprivileged, so every call returns EPERM. The aliases
 and the `lazily` suffix are proved to PARSE and reach umount2(2); MNT_DETACH
 semantics (PRC-20) cannot be observed without a real mount to detach.
 Ran, from the repo root:
   VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm \
   /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox \
   docs/ledger/probes/process-control/PRC-17.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   Unmount set the error flag
   Unmount lazily set the error flag
   the umount alias set the error flag
   the umount alias with lazily set the error flag
   all four spellings compiled and reached the syscall
)
Create a directory called "vf_scratch".
Create a directory called "vf_scratch/process-control".
Create a directory called "vf_scratch/process-control/scratch_unmount".
Unmount "vf_scratch/process-control/scratch_unmount".
On error print "Unmount set the error flag".
Unmount "vf_scratch/process-control/scratch_unmount" lazily.
On error print "Unmount lazily set the error flag".
umount "vf_scratch/process-control/scratch_unmount".
On error print "the umount alias set the error flag".
umount "vf_scratch/process-control/scratch_unmount" lazily.
On error print "the umount alias with lazily set the error flag".
Remove the directory called "vf_scratch/process-control/scratch_unmount".
print "all four spellings compiled and reached the syscall".
